 "pdCallTexts": [
  {
   "deadId": "gen_kpuuvtl",
   "entryDay": 36,
   "cause": "the wild",
   "lines": [
    "d36: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Violet Sandoval is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
    "d36: Nobody's talking much. The fire feels smaller tonight.",
    "d36: 🕯️ Violet Sandoval is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging.",
    "d36: What Violet kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body.",
    "d36: \"Violet's gone.\" Badr looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Violet.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face.",
    "d36: The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Amy blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers.",
    "d36: 📖 LEARNED: Steady Hands (Level 1). Fine work under pressure. Dressing game, stitching wounds, tying snares — no shake.",
    "d36: 📖 LEARNED: Ritual & Meaning (Level 1). Marking the dead matters. Even without religion, ritual holds grief.",
    "d36: 📖 LEARNED: Wound Care (Level 1). Clean it, close it, cover it. Pressure stops bleeding. Clean water is better than dirty hands.",
    "d36: ⚡ TECHNIQUE UNLOCKED: Precise Mend! Your healing knows where to go. +50% effectiveness. (Your knowledge of Wound Care amplifies your field_medicine.)",
    "d36: 📖 LEARNED: Herbal Medicine (Level 1). Willow bark = aspirin. Yarrow stops bleeding. Plantain draws out infection. The pharmacy is outside.",
    "d36: 🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\"",
    "d36: 📖 The Codex turns a page: Violet Sandoval, 36 days. The mantle passes to Amy Castillo.",
    "d36: 🪞 You wake up somebody else. Amy Castillo, 43 — a tattoo artist. Her hands know different work now: Green Whisper.",
    "d36: The village's quarrel was with Violet — and Violet is dead. The sentence doesn't cross the grave. You're someone else now; the docket is empty, but the village remembers.",
